-- title:
--   Segment periods generate the dual of S₂(Γ)
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of finite index (the finite-index hypothesis being supplied as an instance). For each ordered pair $(\tau_0,\tau_1)$ of points of the upper half-plane $\mathbb{H}$, [`ModularCurve.periodAlongOf Γ τ₀ τ₁`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodOf.html#L42) is the $\mathbb{C}$-linear functional on the space `CuspForm Γ 2` of weight-two cusp forms for $\Gamma$ sending $f$ to the interval integral $\int_{0}^{1} f\big(\mathrm{segmentPath}\,\tau_0\,\tau_1\,t\big)\,(\tau_1-\tau_0)\,dt$, where $\mathrm{segmentPath}\,\tau_0\,\tau_1$ is the path in $\mathbb{H}$ joining $\tau_0$ to $\tau_1$ and the integrand is the function `periodIntegrandOf`; additivity in $f$ and compatibility with scalars come from the corresponding properties of the integrand together with interval integrability. The theorem asserts that the additive subgroup of the dual space $\mathrm{Hom}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma),\mathbb{C})$ generated by the set of all these functionals, as $(\tau_0,\tau_1)$ ranges over $\mathbb{H}\times\mathbb{H}$, is the whole dual space. Note that the closure taken is the additive, i.e. $\mathbb{Z}$-linear, closure of the set of segment periods, not merely its $\mathbb{C}$-linear span.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of Jacobi inversion for the compact Riemann surface attached to $\Gamma$: every functional on $S_2(\Gamma)$ is a finite sum and difference of integrals of cusp forms along segments in $\mathbb{H}$. It is used in the construction of the bijective Hecke-equivariant maps from $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the complex modular curve onto the quotient of $S_2(\Gamma)^\vee$ by the period lattice.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_addSubgroupClosure_range_periodAlongOf_eq_top.lean

